GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: strict line/column in SrcLoc
advanceSrcLoc does `c +# 1#` per character. In GHC FastInt is Int#, so the
field is strict for free; under the FastTypes shim it is a lazy Int, and
alexGetChar's `seq` forces only the constructor, so one (+1) thunk per
character accumulates in the column until something forces it. Lines past
~50K columns overflowed the mhs stack. Bang annotations restore the
strictness the original relied on (build/lexer622/FINDINGS.md "Overlay").

--- a/ghc/compiler/basicTypes/SrcLoc.lhs
+++ b/ghc/compiler/basicTypes/SrcLoc.lhs
@@ -52,8 +52,12 @@
 			-- isWiredInName
 
   | SrcLoc	FastString	-- A precise location (file name)
-		FastInt		-- line
-		FastInt		-- column
+		!FastInt	-- line
+		!FastInt	-- column
+		-- mhs: FastInt is a boxed Int here, not Int#, so without the bangs
+		-- advanceSrcLoc leaves one (c +# 1#) thunk per character and the
+		-- column of a token at the end of a long line overflows the
+		-- stack when it is finally forced (seen at ~50K columns).
 
   | UnhelpfulSrcLoc FastString	-- Just a general indication
 
